WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:14.922
Hi! In transformation, you rewrite a sentence in a different way without changing its meaning. Today we'll learn four common types: reported speech, passive, too... to, and inversion.

2
00:00:15.072 --> 00:00:24.810
Reported speech: Amy said, I am tired, becomes Amy said that she was tired. I becomes she, am becomes was, and the speech marks go.

3
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:33.594
Passive: The cat chased the mouse becomes The mouse was chased by the cat. Use a form of be, the past participle, and by.

4
00:00:33.744 --> 00:00:39.426
Too... to: He is so young that he cannot drive becomes He is too young to drive.

5
00:00:39.576 --> 00:00:50.370
Inversion: As soon as I reached home, it rained becomes No sooner had I reached home than it rained. Notice had comes before I, and we use than.

6
00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:59.322
In reported speech, the tense usually moves back: is becomes was, will becomes would, can becomes could, and today becomes that day.

7
00:00:59.472 --> 00:01:05.850
The passive must keep the original tense. If the original is past, use was or were.

8
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:14.106
Another inversion: He sang and also danced becomes Not only did he sing, but he also danced.

9
00:01:14.256 --> 00:01:18.018
Watch out! The window was broke is wrong!

10
00:01:18.168 --> 00:01:26.850
In the passive, the verb after be must be the past participle. Break, broke, broken: the past participle is broken.

11
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:34.290
So write: The window was broken by the ball. Learn your irregular verbs well.

12
00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:44.730
Your turn! Ben said, I will help you. Change it into reported speech. Pause and think.

13
00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:55.410
The answer is: Ben said that he would help me. I becomes he, will becomes would, and you, meaning me, becomes me. Did you get it right?

14
00:01:55.560 --> 00:02:05.418
Another one! The teacher praised Sara. Change it into the passive. Pause and think.

15
00:02:05.568 --> 00:02:12.018
The answer is: Sara was praised by the teacher. Did you get it right?

16
00:02:12.168 --> 00:02:23.466
Here's another! The bag was so heavy that I could not carry it. Rewrite it with too... to. Pause and think.

17
00:02:23.616 --> 00:02:31.770
The answer is: The bag was too heavy for me to carry. No it at the end. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:42.834
One more! He sang. He also danced. Rewrite it beginning with Not only. Pause and think.

19
00:02:42.984 --> 00:02:52.938
The answer is: Not only did he sing, but he also danced. Did goes before he, and sang becomes sing. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:53.088 --> 00:03:09.258
Remember: the meaning must stay the same. In reported speech, move the tense back and change pronouns. The passive uses be plus the past participle. Too... to has no it at the end. And inversion puts had or did before the subject.

21
00:03:09.408 --> 00:03:13.362
Read today's examples aloud!

